WEBVTT

00:00:27.187 --> 00:00:28.979
(ZOUWU GROWLING)

00:00:30.565 --> 00:00:31.774
(NEWT GRUNTING)

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:40.949
JACOB: Hey, uh, Newt, buddy. Uh...

00:00:41.201 --> 00:00:43.243
Tina's up here.
She's all by her lonesome,

00:00:43.411 --> 00:00:45.871
and, uh, maybe you want to come up
and keep her company?

00:00:46.915 --> 00:00:49.625
Uh, I've been looking for food,
and I ain't found any,

00:00:49.793 --> 00:00:51.126
(ZOUWU SNIFFING)

00:00:51.211 --> 00:00:53.212
so I guess I'm gonna go upstairs
and try my luck

00:00:53.380 --> 00:00:55.756
in, oh, I don't know, the attic.

00:00:57.217 --> 00:00:58.550
NEWT: You're all right.

00:00:58.718 --> 00:00:59.968
<i>Relashio.</i>

00:01:06.059 --> 00:01:07.059
Okay.

00:01:19.906 --> 00:01:21.657
She's responded well to the Dittany.

00:01:23.118 --> 00:01:24.618
She was born to run, you see.

00:01:25.286 --> 00:01:27.830
But I think she's...
She's just lacking in confidence.

00:01:29.124 --> 00:01:30.958
Mr. Scamander,
have you got anything in your case

00:01:31.042 --> 00:01:33.210
that might help revive this man?

00:01:33.294 --> 00:01:34.461
I need to question him.

00:01:34.546 --> 00:01:37.005
I think he knows who Credence really is.
And the scars on his hand

00:01:37.173 --> 00:01:39.091
- suggest an Unbreakable Vow.
- An Unbreakable Vow.

00:01:39.259 --> 00:01:40.759
Yeah, I noticed that, too.

00:01:52.605 --> 00:01:53.605
<i>Lumos.</i>

00:01:58.570 --> 00:01:59.570
(GASPS)

00:02:00.864 --> 00:02:02.197
What was that?

00:02:02.365 --> 00:02:04.199
There must be
a Water Dragon in that sewer.

00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:08.162
They carry these parasites,
you see. They, um...

00:02:08.955 --> 00:02:10.831
- Jacob.
- Yeah?

00:02:12.292 --> 00:02:15.502
In my case, in the pocket there,
you'll find a pair of tweezers.

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:16.920
Tweezers?

00:02:17.672 --> 00:02:19.423
- They're thin, pointy...
- Little pointy things.

00:02:19.591 --> 00:02:20.799
JACOB: Yes, I know what tweezers are.

00:02:23.845 --> 00:02:25.554
All right.
You might not want to watch this.

00:02:26.347 --> 00:02:27.598
I can handle it.

00:02:32.562 --> 00:02:33.562
NEWT: Come out.

00:02:33.730 --> 00:02:36.356
- (PARASITE SQUEALING)
- Come on. You're all right.

00:02:36.858 --> 00:02:39.443
- Ew.
- Come on. I got you.

00:02:40.445 --> 00:02:41.612
Jacob, will you take that for me?

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:43.822
Huh. Ugh!

00:02:46.075 --> 00:02:47.075
Calamari.

00:02:49.788 --> 00:02:51.705
Must kill him.

00:02:51.873 --> 00:02:53.207
Who?

00:02:53.291 --> 00:02:54.416
Credence?

00:02:55.794 --> 00:02:57.419
NEWT: It may take him
a few hours to recover.

00:02:57.587 --> 00:02:59.588
That parasite's poison is quite strong.

00:03:01.341 --> 00:03:03.467
I have to go back to the Ministry
with what I've got.

00:03:05.720 --> 00:03:07.221
It's nice to see you again,
Mr. Scamander.

00:03:07.305 --> 00:03:09.389
JACOB: Hey. Hey.
Hold on a second, will ya?

00:03:09.474 --> 00:03:11.225
Hold on. Hold on.

00:03:11.309 --> 00:03:13.393
Wait! Tina.

00:03:17.857 --> 00:03:19.525
You didn't mention salamanders, did you?

00:03:19.692 --> 00:03:22.277
(STAMMERING) No, I didn't.
She just ran. I don't know...

00:03:23.196 --> 00:03:24.988
So you chase after her.

00:03:26.115 --> 00:03:28.742
Tina. Please, just listen to me.

00:03:29.369 --> 00:03:32.412
Mr. Scamander, I need to go talk
to the Ministry.

00:03:32.705 --> 00:03:34.456
I know how you feel about Aurors.

00:03:34.707 --> 00:03:35.999
I may have been a little strong

00:03:36.084 --> 00:03:37.501
in the way that I expressed myself
in that letter.

00:03:37.669 --> 00:03:40.838
What was the exact phrase?
"A bunch of careerist hypocrites"?

00:03:41.047 --> 00:03:42.256
I'm sorry, but I can't admire people

00:03:42.423 --> 00:03:45.551
whose answer to everything that
they fear or misunderstand is "kill it."

00:03:45.718 --> 00:03:47.135
I'm an Auror and I don't.

00:03:47.303 --> 00:03:49.012
Yes, I know.
That's because you've gone middle head.

00:03:51.099 --> 00:03:52.099
Excuse me?

00:03:52.892 --> 00:03:55.185
It's an expression derived from
the three heads of the Runespoor.

00:03:55.270 --> 00:03:56.645
So the middle one is the visionary.

00:03:56.813 --> 00:03:59.106
Now, every Auror in Europe
wants Credence dead, except you.

00:03:59.274 --> 00:04:00.482
You've gone middle head.

00:04:02.110 --> 00:04:04.862
Who else uses that expression,
Mr. Scamander?

00:04:06.364 --> 00:04:07.823
I think it might just be me.

00:04:09.492 --> 00:04:10.909
(WIND WHOOSHING)

00:04:26.259 --> 00:04:29.261
TINA: It's Grindelwald.
He's calling his followers.

